<h1>Same function, two ways to get it: AWS-native vs. open source</h1>
<table class="fig">
<colgroup><col style="width:26%"><col style="width:37%"><col style="width:37%"></colgroup>
<thead><tr><th>FUNCTION</th><th>AWS-NATIVE</th><th>OPEN SOURCE</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Network intrusion detection</td><td>GuardDuty - ML over flow logs, DNS, runtime</td><td>Suricata (signatures) + Falco/eBPF (syscalls)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Central findings &amp; scoring</td><td>Security Hub - ASFF, CIS/PCI-DSS/GDPR score</td><td>Wazuh Manager + self-hosted OpenSearch</td></tr>
<tr><td>Long-term log storage &amp; search</td><td>OpenSearch Service + Security Lake (OCSF)</td><td>Self-hosted OpenSearch / ELK stack</td></tr>
<tr><td>Signed API audit trail</td><td>CloudTrail - 90-day LookupEvents</td><td>auditd + centralized syslog shipping</td></tr>
<tr><td>Configuration drift detection</td><td>AWS Config - rules, auto-remediation</td><td>Checkov (IaC scans) + periodic drift checks</td></tr>
<tr><td>Image / host vulnerability scan</td><td>Inspector - EC2, ECR, Lambda CVEs</td><td>Trivy or Grype (container images)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Web application firewall</td><td>AWS WAF + Shield</td><td>Coraza or ModSecurity + OWASP CRS</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI-assisted triage &amp; modeling</td><td>Bedrock (triage) + SageMaker (custom ML)</td><td>OpenSearch ML Commons + MLflow</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
